# CI rules

- Never put secrets (tokens, keys, passwords) in workflow or CI config. Use the platform secret store (e.g. GitHub Secrets, GitLab CI/CD variables) and reference them as env vars.
- Use explicit, readable job and step names so logs are easy to triage.
- Prefer reusable workflows or includes where supported to avoid duplication.
- Pin actions or use commit SHAs for reproducibility; avoid `@main` or floating tags in production workflows.
- Keep workflows minimal: only the steps needed for the job. Cache dependencies where it speeds up runs.
- **Dev/prod split:** Prefer separate workflows for dev (auto on push) and prod (manual only). Use different env vars and deploy paths. Reference pn-ci-dev-prod-split when scaffolding deploy workflows.
